// Title: Taskkill Symantec Endpoint Protection
// Sigma ID: 35bd2ff5-4d47-42e0-b11b-778e9d439e93
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Ilya Krestinichev, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-13 | Modified: 2026-11-06
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects one of the possible scenarios for disabling Symantec Endpoint Protection. Symantec
//   Endpoint Protection antivirus software services incorrectly implement the protected service
//   mechanism. As a result, the NT AUTHORITY/SYSTEM user can execute the taskkill /im command
//   several times ccSvcHst.exe /f, thereby killing the process belonging to the service, and thus
//   shutting down the service.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/37525
//   - https://community.spiceworks.com/topic/2195015-batch-script-to-uninstall-symantec-endpoint-protection
//   - https://community.broadcom.com/symantecenterprise/communities/community-home/digestviewer/viewthread?MessageKey=6ce94b67-74e1-4333-b16f-000b7fd874f0&CommunityKey=1ecf5f55-9545-44d6-b0f4-4e4a7f5f5e68&tab=digestviewer
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ebd26c2d9cd57dc9489faa1f1346577be9947747/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_taskkill_sep.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "taskkill" and ProcessCommandLine contains " /F " and ProcessCommandLine contains " /IM " and ProcessCommandLine contains "ccSvcHst.exe"
